    "note": "Reviewed every direct build, runtime, optional development and Node registry candidate, including candidates outside declared upper bounds. All current latest releases satisfy existing ranges and Python 3.14; no dependency manifest change is needed. Validation environment already contains build 1.6.1, hypothesis 6.168.0, packaging 26.3, ruff 0.16.6 and pydantic 2.13.5. Reviewed official release notes: https://github.com/pypa/build/releases/tag/1.6.1 and its 1.6.0 changelog (new CLI features and removed BuildBackendException.exc_info are not used here); https://hypothesis.readthedocs.io/en/latest/changelog.html (date generation and shrink/cache fixes); https://github.com/pypa/packaging/releases/tag/26.3 (specifier and metadata handling); https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/releases/tag/0.16.6 (lint fixes); https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/releases/tag/v2.13.5 (validator GC and smart union fixes). Repository fast gate passes with these installed versions. Relocation, standalone no-site-packages executable and version contract targets passed; explicit MariaDB 10.11.11 resident, relocated-library reuse and gallery-removal E2E passed (3 cases). The integration gate will additionally run bounded offline pytest, Lean, finite small TLC, sdist/wheel build and installed CLI/pipeline smoke. Existing upper bounds remain the tested major or compatibility lanes; no workaround or new pin was introduced.",
